  {
   "n": 5,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +1 / -0.33",
   "html": "<p>\n\tWhich of the following statements is/are true?<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : In a lattice every two elements need not have both join and meet.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : In a distributive lattice L, a given element can have atmost one complement.</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>\n\tOnly <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>\n\tBoth <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "Neither of them"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "B"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "B",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 1,
    "neg": 0.33
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(b)<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> is false because poset would be called as lattice iff any two elements must have both meet and join.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> is true because if any element has complement then it must be unique.</p>"
  },
