  {
   "n": 19,
   "type": "MCQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • COMPUTER SCIENCE • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>\n\tConsider statements:<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : A finite lattice is always bounded.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : Complemented lattice is a proper subset of bounded lattice.<br />\n\t<em>S</em><sub>3</sub> : A bounded and complemented lattice may or may not be a distributive lattice.<br />\n\tWhich of the following is/are true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "<p>\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "<p>\n\t<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>\n\t<em>S</em><sub>1</sub>, <em>S</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>3</sub></p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "D",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>\n\t(d)<br />\n\t&bull; A lattice is bounded iff the lattice has a greatest and a least element.<br />\n\t&there4; A finite lattice is always bounded.<br />\n\t&bull; Complemented lattice is defined only for bounded lattice. A bounded lattice is complemented iff atleast one complement of every element exist in lattice. An element should one or more complements.<br />\n\t&bull; A complemented lattice is distributive iff every element has a unique complement.</p>"
  },
